Sira: Any news from the other villages, dad?
Dad: They're struggling to keep the fire from spreading too.
Dad: There's simply not enough water.
Dad: The haze is thickening.
Dad: More people are getting sick because of it.
Dad: Don't spend too much time in the forest, Sira.
Sira: Some of the animals can't save themselves, dad.
Sira: Someone has to do it.